<div class="eyebrow">Business Analysis · Self-driven case study</div>
<h1>Food Delivery Order &amp; Payment System</h1>
<p class="lead">A case study exploring how clearer requirements and a more reliable ordering and payment workflow could reduce customer confusion, payment-related drop-offs, and avoidable support requests.</p>
<div class="tags"><span class="tag">Requirements Analysis</span><span class="tag">BRD / FRD</span><span class="tag">User Stories</span><span class="tag">Process Mapping</span><span class="tag">UAT</span><span class="tag">REST API / JSON</span><span class="tag">SQL &amp; Power BI concepts</span></div>
<div class="grid" style="margin-top:24px">
<div class="card"><div class="label">Project summary</div><h2>Business problem</h2><p>When a payment fails, customers may be unsure whether an order was placed. Support teams also need a clear way to identify payment and order statuses. This case study defines a proposed workflow for payment handling, order confirmation, tracking and refunds.</p><p><strong>My approach:</strong> define the problem and scope, identify stakeholders, document business rules, write user stories, map the process and outline UAT scenarios.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="label">At a glance</div><div class="statgrid"><div class="stat"><strong>Role</strong><span>BA case study</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>Domain</strong><span>Food delivery</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>Focus</strong><span>Order &amp; payment</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>Outputs</strong><span>Requirements &amp; test cases</span></div></div></div>
</div></div>
<section class="wrap"><h2 class="section-title">1. Objectives and scope</h2><p class="sub">Keep the solution focused on the customer journey from cart to confirmation and status updates.</p><div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>Business objectives</h3><ul><li>Make payment outcomes clear to customers.</li><li>Define when an order can be sent to a restaurant.</li><li>Provide consistent order-status updates.</li><li>Make cancellation and refund handling easier to track.</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Scope boundaries</h3><p><strong>In scope:</strong> menu browsing, cart, checkout, UPI/card/COD payment, confirmation, tracking, cancellation and refund status.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> restaurant onboarding, delivery routing algorithms, payroll and accounting.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap"><h2 class="section-title">2. Stakeholder analysis</h2><p class="sub">Stakeholder needs inform the requirements and acceptance criteria.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Stakeholder</th><th>Primary need</th><th>BA consideration</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Customer</td><td>Clear payment outcome and order status</td><td>Readable messages, retry path, order history</td></tr>
<tr><td>Restaurant partner</td><td>Receive valid orders without delay</td><td>Send order after the required payment condition</td></tr>
<tr><td>Delivery partner</td><td>Accurate delivery and order details</td><td>Reliable status and address data</td></tr>
<tr><td>Payment gateway</td><td>Secure transaction processing</td><td>Handle success, failure, pending and timeout responses</td></tr>
<tr><td>Product / operations</td><td>Fewer complaints and better completion rates</td><td>Track failure reasons and order funnel metrics</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="wrap"><h2 class="section-title">3. Key business rules</h2><p class="sub">Illustrative rules for the proposed solution; validate them with stakeholders before implementation.</p><div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>BR-01 · Restaurant availability</h3><p>An order cannot be submitted when the restaurant is closed or an item is unavailable.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>BR-02 · Payment confirmation</h3><p>For prepaid orders, send the order to the restaurant only after payment is confirmed. COD follows its approved path.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>BR-03 · Failed payment</h3><p>Show a clear outcome and allow retry or another payment method. Retry limits must be agreed with product and payment teams.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>BR-04 · Refund tracking</h3><p>For an eligible cancellation, create a refund request and show its status. Timing depends on provider rules and policy.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap"><h2 class="section-title">4. AS-IS vs TO-BE process</h2><p class="sub">A high-level view of the problem and proposed improvement.</p><div class="grid">
<div class="card"><div class="label">AS-IS · Problem state</div><div class="flow"><div class="step">Customer checks out</div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="step">Payment fails</div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="step">Unclear outcome</div></div><p>Potential gap: the customer may not know whether to retry, and support may need to investigate manually.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="label">TO-BE · Proposed state</div><div class="flow"><div class="step">Customer checks out</div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="step">Payment result checked</div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="step">Confirm or offer retry</div></div><p>Improvement: show clear status, prevent duplicate orders and send the order when the applicable payment condition is met.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap"><h2 class="section-title">5. Sample user stories</h2><p class="sub">Stories capture user needs; acceptance criteria make expected behaviour testable.</p><div class="grid">
<div class="card"><div class="label">US-01 · Cart</div><h3>Review cart before checkout</h3><p><em>As a customer, I want to add menu items to my cart so that I can review quantities and prices before payment.</em></p><ul><li>Available items are added with correct price and quantity.</li><li>Changing quantity recalculates the total.</li><li>Cart follows the product rule for items from different restaurants.</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><div class="label">US-02 · Payment</div><h3>Know whether payment succeeded</h3><p><em>As a customer, I want a clear payment result so that I know whether my order has been placed.</em></p><ul><li>On success, show confirmation and order ID.</li><li>On failure, show a clear message and retry/alternate method.</li><li>Pending payments do not create duplicate orders.</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><div class="label">US-03 · Tracking</div><h3>Track order progress</h3><p><em>As a customer, I want to view my order status so that I understand delivery progress.</em></p><ul><li>Display the latest valid status.</li><li>Trigger configured notifications for key status changes.</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><div class="label">US-04 · Restaurant</div><h3>Receive confirmed order details</h3><p><em>As a restaurant partner, I want valid order details so that I can begin preparation without confusion.</em></p><ul><li>Display items, quantities and special instructions.</li><li>Do not send a prepaid order until payment confirmation.</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap"><h2 class="section-title">6. Data mapping and API understanding</h2><p class="sub">Illustrative mapping only. Engineering would confirm final field names, types and schemas.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Business field</th><th>Example system field</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Order identifier</td><td><code>order_id</code></td><td>String</td><td>Unique order reference</td></tr><tr><td>Customer identifier</td><td><code>customer_id</code></td><td>String</td><td>Links order to customer</td></tr><tr><td>Items</td><td><code>items[]</code></td><td>Array</td><td>Item ID, quantity and price</td></tr><tr><td>Payment status</td><td><code>payment_status</code></td><td>Enum</td><td>SUCCESS, FAILED or PENDING</td></tr><tr><td>Order status</td><td><code>order_status</code></td><td>Enum</td><td>Tracks order lifecycle</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3 style="margin-top:22px">Example JSON payload</h3><pre><code>{
  "order_id": "ORD12345",
  "customer_id": "CUST789",
  "items": [
    { "item_id": "ITM001", "qty": 2, "price": 150 }
  ],
  "payment_status": "SUCCESS",
  "order_status": "CONFIRMED"
}</code></pre><div class="note"><strong>Technical BA perspective:</strong> clarify field meaning, allowed values, validation rules, error scenarios and dependencies with engineering. This example is not a live API integration.</div></section>
<section class="wrap"><h2 class="section-title">7. UAT test scenarios</h2><p class="sub">UAT checks whether the solution meets agreed business requirements from an end-user perspective.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Scenario</th><th>Expected result</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>UAT-01</td><td>Checkout while restaurant is closed</td><td>Checkout is blocked and a clear message appears.</td></tr><tr><td>UAT-02</td><td>Payment fails</td><td>Failure is shown; retry or alternate payment option is available per policy.</td></tr><tr><td>UAT-03</td><td>Payment is pending and customer retries</td><td>System checks transaction status and prevents duplicate handling.</td></tr><tr><td>UAT-04</td><td>Eligible paid order is cancelled</td><td>Refund request is created and its status is visible.</td></tr><tr><td>UAT-05</td><td>Order status changes</td><td>Latest valid status appears and configured notification is triggered.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="wrap"><h2 class="section-title">8. Success measures to validate</h2><p class="sub">These are proposed KPIs, not measured results. A real implementation needs a baseline and post-launch data.</p><div class="grid3">
<div class="card"><h3>Checkout conversion</h3><p>Share of checkout sessions resulting in a completed order.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Payment failure rate</h3><p>Share of payment attempts that fail, segmented by method and reason.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Support contact rate</h3><p>Payment/order-related support contacts per defined number of orders.</p></div></div></section>
